title: Te_Start_Day1
position: -48,-437
---

<<declare $te_clown to false>>
<<declare $te_waddles to false>>
<<declare $te_circus to false>>

<<if $te_clown is false and $te_waddles is false and $te_circus is false>>
    ???: Knock knock!
        -> You: Who's there?
            Teddy: Teddy! *jazz hands*
            You: *clap excitedly*
        -> You: I don't have time for jokes.
            Teddy: Teddy... Oh, darn it. I'm sorry.
            Teddy: I was really looking forward to doing jazz hands if you had chosen the other option.
            You: My apologies, Teddy.
    You: I'm investigating the recent murder the late Mr. Waddles. Surely the news of his untimely passing have already reached you.
    Teddy: Oh yes, Eduard told me about it when we were playing cards earlier. I won you know!
        -> You: Very well ...
        -> You: I'm pleased to hear that.
    Teddy: I'm really good at playing cards. My favorite is Memory but I also enjoy...
    You: Would you be willing to answer a few question concerning the circumstances of Mr. Waddles passing?
    Teddy: Oh. *he looks a little disappointed* Alright.
<<elseif $te_clown is true or $te_waddles is true or $te_circus is true>>
    Teddy: I need to leave soon. Eduard is probably already looking for me.
<<endif>>
    -> What exactly do you do as a... *checks notes* a clown? <<if $te_clown is false>>
        <<jump Te_Clown>>
    -> Were you close to the late Mr. Waddles. <<if $te_waddles is false>>
        <<jump Te_Waddles>>
    -> Why did you join the circus? <<if $te_circus is false>>
        <<jump Te_Circus>>
    -> You: That should suffice for today. Thank you for your time.
        Teddy: We should do that again tomorrow! It made me feel kind of important *he looks really proud*.
===


title: Te_Clown
---
<<set $te_clown to true>>

Teddy: Every fun thing imaginable! I make balloon animals and spend time with my best friend Eduard and I make all the people happy and sometimes I even get to eat cake! *his eyes light up*
You: You seem to be spending a lot of time with Mr. Eduard.
Teddy: Yes, we are the greatest clown duo west of the great sea. And we even get to share a wagon! Isn't that incredible?
Teddy: Eduard always tells lots of funny jokes when we hang out.
Teddy: But he is not just funny, he is also very smart and has way too many books to even count.
<<if $russian_classic is true>>
    You: \[weird russian classic\] Speaking of books, do you know if this one might belong to Eduard as well? <<if $russian_classic is true>>
    Teddy: It certainly looks <i>smart</i>, but I'm not sure if it belongs to Eduard. *he starts pondering*
    Teddy: Hmmm.. *still pondering*
    Teddy: I think... *he seems to have made up his mind*
    Teddy: No, sorry. I can't read.
    You: Oh, don't worry about it. We move on to the next question then.
    <<jump Te_Start_Day1>>
<<else>>
    <<jump Te_Start_Day1>>
<<endif>>
===

title: Te_Waddles
---
<<declare $te_enemies to false>>
<<declare $te_parting_letter to false>>
<<declare $te_observations to false>>

<<set $te_waddles to true>>

<<if $te_enemies is false and $te_parting_letter is false and $te_observations is false>>
    Teddy: Not as close as I am to Eduard, but we were friendly.
<<elseif $te_enemies is false or $te_parting_letter is false or $te_observations is false>>
    Teddy: I'm getting a little hungry. But I think I can manage a few more questions.
<<else>>
    <<jump Te_Start_Day1>>
<<endif>>
    -> You: Did the deceased have any enemies that you are aware of? <<if $te_enemies is false>>
        <<jump Te_Enemies>>
    -> You: \[parting letter\] Did Mr. Waddles appear fulfilled by his position as a trumpeter to you? <<if $te_parting_letter is false and $parting_letter is true>>
        <<jump Te_PartingLetter>>
    -> You: Did you notice any unusual behaviors from Mr.Waddles yesterday? <<if $te_observations is false>>
        <<jump Te_Observations>>
===

title: Te_Circus
---
<<set $te_circus to true>>

Teddy: Oh, I love to tell that story! So it was a warm afternoon in august.
Teddy: No wait! It was february and the forecast had just announced that the hail wouldn't be stopping anytime soon.
Teddy: Anyways... where was I? Oh, right. So I had just woken up from my midday slumber when...
You: I'll take the abbreviated version if possible.
Teddy: Oh, of course! I saw a flyer and thought that it looked fun.
<<jump Te_Start_Day1>>
===

title: Te_Enemies
---
<<set $te_enemies to true>>

<<declare $te_enemies_reason to false>>
<<declare $te_enemies_teddy to false>>

<<if $te_enemies_reason is false and $te_enemies_teddy is false>>
    Teddy: Enemies? What do you mean?
    You: Did anyone wish ill upon him?
    Teddy: Oh, why didn't you just say that in the first place? If you put it that way, almost everyone was his enemy.
<<elseif $te_enemies_reason is false or $te_enemies_teddy is false>>
    Teddy: I'm sorry, I don't know what else to say about that.
<<else>>
    <<jump Te_Waddles>>
<<endif>>
    -> You: Why do you think everyone disliked the late Mr. Waddles? <<if $te_enemies_reason is false>>
        <<jump Te_Enemies_Reason>>
    -> You: Would you consider yourself one of those enemies. <<if $te_enemies_teddy is false>>
        <<jump Te_Enemies_Teddy>>
===

title: Te_PartingLetter
---
<<set $te_parting_letter to true>>

Teddy: He used to look at his trumpet really lovingly so he must have been, right?
<<jump Te_Waddles>>
===

title: Te_Observations
---
<<set $te_observations to true>>

<<declare $te_supposition to false>>
<<declare $te_suspect to false>>
<<declare $te_day to false>>
<<declare $te_performance to false>>

<<if $te_supposition is false and $te_suspect is false and $te_day is false and $te_performance is false>>
    Teddy: You're right! I did see him do something weird yesterday. Or rather didn't see him do anything. 
    Teddy: I didn't see him all day up until our evening performance was about to start. He must have been in his wagon the whole time.
<<elseif $te_supposition is false or $te_suspect is false or $te_day is false or $te_performance is false>>
    Teddy: *stomach grumbles*
<<else>>
    <<jump Te_Questions>>
<<endif>>
    -> You: Do you have any idea what he could have been doing in there? <<if $te_supposition is false>>
        <<jump Te_Supposition>>
    -> You: Did you see anyone entering or leaving the wagon of Mr. Waddles throughout the day? <<if $te_suspect is false>>
        <<jump Te_Suspect>>
    -> You: What have you been busying yourself with yesterday? <<if $te_day is false>>
        <<jump Te_Day>>
    -> You: Did anything unusual happen during last nights performance? <<if $te_performance is false>>
        <<jump Te_Performance>>
===

title: Te_Enemies_Reason
---
<<set $te_enemies_reason to true>>

Teddy: Hmm, good question. He had a weird sense of humor. Maybe they didn't understand his jokes.
<<jump Te_Enemies>>
===

title: Te_Enemies_Teddy
---
<<set $te_enemies_teddy to true>>

Teddy: Could I maybe talk to Eduard before I choose?
Teddy: I like to make sure that we are on the same page when it comes to those things.
<<jump Te_Enemies>>
===

title: Te_Supposition
---
<<set $te_supposition to true>>

Teddy: Hmmm... I believe he could have done anything if he put his mind to it, really.
Teddy: But if I had to say, he was probably polishing his trumpet. He liked to do that.
<<jump Te_Observations>>
===

title: Te_Suspect
---
<<set $te_suspect to true>>

Teddy: Not that I know of, no. But maybe I did see someone and forgot.
Teddy: Would I be in trouble if I forgot?
<<jump Te_Observations>>
===

title: Te_Day
---
<<set $te_day to true>>

Teddy: I ran into Poppet right after I woke up and she gifted me a sandwich. Then I took the sandwich back to the wagon and shared it with Eduard.
Teddy: Wait, I forgot to tell you how I left the wagon to begin with. 
Teddy: It was through the door.
Teddy: Alright, now back to where I left off. Eduard and I spent most of the day practicing our new routine. 
Teddy: Oh and Eduard was taking notes I think.
Teddy: Then I tried to repair some costumes but I gave up on that quickly.
Teddy: Would you like for me to demonstrate the routine to you?
You: No, that was quite sufficient.
<<jump Te_Observations>>
===

title: Te_Performance
---
<<set $te_performance to true>>

Teddy: I'm not so sure, if anything weird happened during the performance. But the monkeys acted strange when I met them backstage after the show.
You: Can you specify further?
Teddy: I can't put my finger on it, but they certainly acted <i>weeiird</i>. *he squints his eyes in suspicion*.
<<jump Te_Observations>>
===

title: Te_Questions
---
<<declare $te_honey_brittle to false>>
<<declare $te_costumes to false>>
<<declare $te_alibi to false>>

<<if $te_honey_brittle is false and $te_costumes is false and $te_alibi is false>>
    Teddy: Would you like to hear a joke?
    You: I'm afraid we've got not time to waste.
    Teddy: Oh, right.
<<elseif $te_honey_brittle is false or $te_costumes is false or $te_alibi is false>>
    Teddy: How about now? Do we have time for a joke now?
<<elseif ($honey_brittle is false or $te_honey_brittle is true) and $te_costumes is true and $te_alibi is true>>
    <<jump Te_Waddles>>
<<endif>>
-> You: \[honey brittle\] Do you know what this is? <<if $te_honey_brittle is false and $honey_brittle is true>>
    <<jump Te_HoneyBrittle>>
-> You: You mentioned the repairing of costumes earlier. Am I correct to assume, that the clothing rack was in your possession until it was returned to the late Mr. Waddles? <<if $te_costumes is false>>
    <<jump Te_Costumes>>
-> You: What were you doing during the time of the murder? <<if $te_alibi is false>>
    <<jump Te_Alibi>>
===

title: Te_HoneyBrittle
---
<<set $te_honey_brittle to true>>
Teddy: Oh golly, did Lady Poppet give those to you? I haven't had them in so long.
    -> You: No, I found them at the crime scene.
       Teddy: That's weird. They do certainly look like the ones that Poppet makes.
    -> You: Yes and I'll let you have them if you tell me a funny joke.
       Teddy: Knock knock.
       -> You: Who is there?
           Teddy: It's me, honey!
           Teddy: ...
           Teddy: You need to say "honey who?"
           -> You: *Exhales* Honey who?
               Teddy: HONEY BRITTLE!!! *chuckles*
               -> *give him the honey_brittle*
                   Teddy: *lunges for the honey brittle and starts chewing* Wou aw won wucky beaw, Teddy.
               -> *return the honey brittle back to your suitcase*
                   Teddy: Oh, darn it.
<<jump Te_Questions>>
===

title: Te_Costumes
---
<<set $te_costumes to true>>

Teddy: Yes, that's right. We take turns you know! It's one of Waddle's jokes that no one finds funny.
    -> You: Please elaborate
        Teddy: The manager told Waddles to do the costume work, but he just took the wagon and all of us take turns doing the work now.
        Teddy: It's not fair at all, but he threatened to poke holes in all of my pointy hats if I tell on him.
        Teddy: Puh *he looks upset*. And now I'm stuck trying to sew with those useless paws.
<<jump Te_Questions>>
===

title: Te_Alibi
---
<<set $te_alibi to true>>

Teddy: Eduard and I were hanging out and I was practicing my juggling!
    -> You: Do you recall what Eduard was doing in the meantime?
        Teddy: He was reading one of his smart books I think. He tends to do that.
<<jump Te_Questions>>
===